@TITLE@ QilinRecomp for macOS (Apple silicon and Intel)
========================================================

@FULL_TITLE@ (@STUDIO@), recompiled to run natively: the game's own program
translated into C++ and compiled for your Mac, drawn with Vulkan (through
MoltenVK, which comes with the app).

No game data is included. You need your own copy of the game: @RELEASE@,
extracted into a folder with Dolphin.


Your game folder
----------------
In Dolphin, right-click the game in the list, choose Properties, open the
Filesystem tab, right-click the disc at the top and choose Extract Entire
Disc, and pick an empty folder. The folder you need is the one holding
"sys" and "files": if Dolphin made a DATA folder inside the one you picked,
it is that DATA folder.


Playing
-------
1. Drag @TITLE@.app onto Applications (in this disk image's window). Building
   the game needs about 2 GB free.
2. Open @TITLE@ from Applications. The first time, macOS stops it, because
   the app isn't signed by an Apple developer account (see below):
   - open System Settings, then Privacy & Security;
   - scroll down to Security, where it says "@TITLE@ was blocked to protect
     your Mac" (or "... was blocked from use because it is not from an
     identified developer");
   - click Open Anyway, then Open Anyway again in the window that appears,
     and confirm with your password or Touch ID.
   macOS asks only once. (On macOS 14, right-clicking the app in Finder and
   choosing Open does the same.)
3. The game is compiled with Apple's own compiler, free from Apple (its
   licence doesn't let it come with this download). If your Mac doesn't have
   it yet, the app says so: click "Install Apple's command line tools",
   follow Apple's installer (a few minutes), then click "Check again".
4. Click "Choose your extracted disc" and pick the folder above, or drag it
   onto the window. It tells you straight away if it is the wrong game,
   another region or another revision.
5. Wait for the first build: a few minutes. Your game files never leave your
   Mac.
6. Click Play. The window hides while the game runs.

After that, the app remembers your folder, and Play starts the game straight
away. After an update it builds the game again first, recompiling only what
changed.

The game's output is in run.log and run-errors.log, and the build's in
build.log, all in ~/Library/Application Support/qilin/@GAME@/work (in Finder:
Go, Go to Folder); the game's own log is punchout.log, one folder up. Send
them when reporting a problem.

About "Open Anyway": the app is signed only by itself ("ad hoc"), not by an
Apple developer account, so Gatekeeper can't name who made it. Check that you
downloaded it from the project's GitHub releases page (below) before you
open it. Nothing in it changes that check or works around it.

Needs: macOS 14.5 (Sonoma) or newer, on an Apple silicon or Intel Mac, and
Apple's command line tools from Xcode 16 or newer, which need that macOS
(the app checks; older tools are updated with System Settings, General,
Software Update). Graphics go through MoltenVK, Vulkan over Apple's Metal.


Controls
--------
A Wii Remote held sideways, buttons only (no motion controls).

  Controller           Keyboard        Wii Remote
  D-pad, left stick    arrows          dodge, duck, block
  B                    Z               1 (left punch)
  A                    X               2 (right punch)
  X or Y               C, Space        A (Star Punch, OK)
  Start / Back         Return / Delete + / -
  Guide                H               HOME
  right stick          mouse or trackpad  the pointer (click is A)

Back + Start together, or F1 or Esc: the settings menu (the game pauses):
controls (set by pressing them), a second player for Head-to-Head, the
picture (size, a CRT look, internal resolution, filtering), full screen,
the game's language and widescreen. Option+Return, F11 or the window's
green button: full screen. On a Mac keyboard F1, F3 and F11 may need the fn
key. F3: the frame rate.

Settings, saves and the game's log are kept in ~/Library/Application
Support/qilin/@GAME@, with the folder you chose, the build (work) and its
cache of compiled files (build-cache).


What's in the app
-----------------
Right-click @TITLE@.app, Show Package Contents:

Contents/MacOS/Play @TITLE@       chooses your extracted disc, builds the
                                  game (once) and starts it
Contents/Resources/kit/qilin      the recompiler: turns the disc's @BOOT@
                                  into C++
Contents/Resources/kit/plan.tsv   which parts of the game are recompiled,
                                  and which run natively
Contents/Resources/kit/lib, include
                                  the prebuilt rest of the game: its
                                  runtime, the renderer, sound, the window
                                  and controls (SDL3), the menu (Dear ImGui)
Contents/Resources/kit/files.txt  every file this release holds (see below)
Contents/Frameworks/libMoltenVK.dylib
                                  MoltenVK: Vulkan over Metal (Khronos)
Contents/Resources/LICENSES       the licences of everything included

The game itself (@EXE@), built from your disc, is in the work folder above,
not in the app: the app is never changed by building.

Source, changes and issues: https://github.com/Qilin1066/PunchOutWii--QilinRecomp


Updates and recovery
--------------------
"Check for updates" in the app asks GitHub for a newer release of
@FULL_TITLE@ (it sends nothing about you or your Mac). If there is one, it
downloads the disk image, copies the new app beside this one and swaps it
in, then starts again and builds the game for the new version. If anything
fails on the way, the old version is left as it was. The app must be
somewhere you can write to for that (Applications is, for an
administrator): run from the disk image itself, it can't update. You can
also drag a new download's app over this one in Applications: it finds your
folder and the cache by itself. Your saves and settings are never in the
app, so nothing of yours is touched.

The game is compiled for this Mac's processor; on another Mac, it is built
again. Compiled files come from the cache when nothing they're made from has
changed. A failed build leaves the working game as it was; the one before a
new build is kept as work/@EXE@.previous until the new one has run and
closed normally. "Build again from scratch" compiles everything anew.

Before the game writes a save, the copy it replaces is kept: up to five of
each save file. The settings menu's Game page, Previous saves, restores one
and restarts (backing up the current save first).
